# HG2-B (data(D), item 3): in Change `x := x + 1` is the call's local, and `data(To)` runs From's data over To (a declaration
# of a visible name: the local). From\x stays 6 (short_result 6, pinned 7); FromParts\x stays 16 (parts_result 16, pinned 17).
# Results written through data\ (rule Б). Observation: explicit writes in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract; #call-frame-20261115).
# of a visible name: the local).
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the inner `data(To)` is the removed form (a data record launched over other data). The same
# property is carried by the structural link: Change is written in From and in FromParts and launched over its parent
# (`From\Change()`, `FromParts\Change()`); the inner launch is the relay record of To, `To\Relay()`. Every bare write
# `x := x + 1` is reached and writes the local of its launch (#call-frame-20261115): the local is read out by an
# explicit write right after it (change_local 17 -- the local of FromParts, 16 + 1; relay_local 1 -- the local of
# To's relay, 0 + 1), and no source changes: From\x stays 6 (short_result 6), FromParts\x stays 16 (parts_result 16),
# To\x stays 0 (to_x 0).
# Norm: the book #structural-call (the data is parent(C)), #call-frame-20261115 (no write-back of a bare write).
Observed:
    int: short_result 0
    int: parts_result 0
    int: to_x 0
    int: change_local 0
    int: relay_local 0
end: Observed
To:
    int: x 0
    Relay:
        x := x + 1
        Observed\relay_local := x
    end: Relay
end: To
From:
    int: x 6
    Change:
        x := x + 1
        Observed\change_local := x
        To\Relay()
    end: Change
end: From
FromParts:
    int: x 16
    Change:
        x := x + 1
        Observed\change_local := x
        To\Relay()
    end: Change
end: FromParts
Main:
    From\Change()
    FromParts\Change()
    Observed\short_result := From\x
    Observed\parts_result := FromParts\x
    Observed\to_x := To\x
